{
  "schema": "cutie.strategy_kernel_conformance.v2c",
  "source_of_truth": "JES21-B3b 二期 IMPL §3.3 / K1 (2026-10-25): StrategySpec v2 ema / macd / rolling_zscore; Server (S1) and Provider share this fixture verbatim",
  "note": "All series use a fixed 1h (3600s) step starting at ts=0. `value: null` in `input` is a genuine mid-stream gap; `expected: null` is a frame the primitive must report missing. Arithmetic is cutie.decimal128.v1 (34 significant digits, ROUND_HALF_EVEN), every operation rounded. ema(window_bars=N): alpha=2/(N+1); seed at the N-th fetched value = (x_0+...+x_{N-1})/N summed left to right; afterwards ema_t = alpha*x_t + (1-alpha)*ema_{t-1}; fewer than N values -> missing; a gap breaks the chain irrecoverably (same rule as v2 rsi_wilder). macd(fast,slow,signal,output): line_t = ema(fast)_t - ema(slow)_t from the slow seed onward; signal = ema(signal) over the line series, seeded from the first line value; hist_t = line_t - signal_t; output selects line/signal/hist; a gap breaks all three irrecoverably. rolling_zscore(window_bars=N): exactly N values ending at x_t, mean = sum/N, population variance = sum((v-mean)*(v-mean))/N, z = (x_t-mean)/sqrt(variance); variance 0 -> missing (never 0); a gap inside the window -> missing until the window slides past it. Bollinger templates use population stdev (rolling(...).std(ddof=0)), so `rolling_zscore gte k` / `lte -k` is exactly touching the k-sigma band.",
  "sha256": "5f8761de46ce2d0094c10f35c6d64928f8275e6ac32cad0049f0f65c2097c038",
